  "text": "The user is asking me to write a plain-text paragraph about how rivers shape valleys, approximately 150 words long. This is a straightforward writing task that doesn't require any tools. I should just provide the text directly.\n\n\nRivers are the primary sculptors of valleys, carving their channels through relentless erosion over millions of years. As water flows downhill, it picks up sediment—sand, gravel, and rock fragments—that act like sandpaper, grinding away at the riverbed and banks. This continuous abrasion deepens and widens the channel, creating the characteristic V-shaped cross-section of youthful valleys. The river's velocity determines its erosive power: fast-moving water in steep mountainous regions cuts downward rapidly, while slower streams in flatter areas focus on lateral erosion, meandering back and forth and gradually broadening the valley floor. Tributaries feed the main river, contributing additional erosive force and carrying sediment from side valleys into the main channel. Over geological time, these processes transform rugged landscapes into deep, winding valleys with steep sides and broad floodplains. Flooding events periodically deposit nutrient-rich sediment across the valley floor, creating fertile plains ideal for agriculture. Ultimately, the river's persistent flow, combined with the physical force of transported sediment, gradually reshapes the earth's surface, creating the valleys we recognize today.",
